Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

THE ANSWER (9h cap, 110 games, margin = 80% of usable): the largest MEASURED
budget that fits is 2000, and 2000 survives all three cost levels. 4000 fits
centrally but its cost is EXTRAPOLATED. At the 6h reading it tightens to 1000
central / 400 conservative. Critical N at 9h: 233 games at b400, 141 at b2000.
MAX_ACTIONS is UNTOUCHED — this measures and reports; the flag is the operator's.

WHAT DECIDES IT is a decomposition nobody had measured: per-game LATENCY rises
1.81x at K=2 (6 matched game-seed pairs, two-sided p=0.0312 at a 0.0312 floor)
while total THROUGHPUT does NOT degrade (114.5 -> 108.6 s/game; matched-set ratio
median 0.9735, per-seed 0.948/0.999), because GPU 1 is already 76.7% busy with a
SINGLE game. A wall-clock cap divides throughput, not latency, so the prior
conservative reading (uncontended latency x 1.72 x game count) double-counts. The
prior fitted cost model is tested and its crossing point voided: mechanism already
falsified by the sibling, level 1.68-2.11x high.

A CONCURRENCY CEILING IS HIT FIRST. At K=4 the frozen generator died in BOTH
seeds (8/8 cells: generator_healthy_after False on all 8, zero LLM responses on 3
-- every cell still exiting 0 with a complete 400-action run). A matched
configuration test isolates the mechanism: at n_ctx=32768 (8192/slot, room for
prompt + the agent's own 4096 max_tokens) the SAME cells are 4/4 VALID against
0/4 at the shipped 16384, and K=4 throughput is flat there too (116.2 s/game vs
K=1's 100.7). Reported as a MECHANISM, not a recommendation.

WHAT THE RAISE BUYS, in the unit that pays: +7 median wins/seed for +0.0541 score
points out of 2500 (offline unit, exact, 3/3 seeds positive, p-floor 0.25 =
UNDERPOWERED). In the GATEWAY-charged unit the full-corpus delta is smaller than
the attribution estimator's own error, so its SIGN is not resolvable there; on the
11 cells with exact attribution at both budgets it is +0.0021. The offline unit
also OVERSTATES the raise: M2 optimism grows 2.97% -> 5.54% as the reset charge
grows with the budget.

WALL CLOCK DOES NOT BIND at the score-maximising budget at the 9h cap, so the
adaptive early-stop lever is NOT revived — and its trade curves say why it would
not be free anyway: 81-92% of actions earn no score, but a start-window saving
39.4% of them loses 24.2% of wins, and preserving every observed subsequent
level-up needs a window 22x the game's own first level-up cost.

Nine gates, each with a computed non-vacuity witness. G1's witness is that this
probe's OWN first launch was blocked by it when the resolver returned the iGPU
build; G7 caught a reserved-key misuse in this very analyser; G9's counterfactual
shows that averaging the dead-generator arm in would have reported concurrency as
a large throughput WIN. A rebuild-determinism check caught the checksum including
a build timestamp, which is now excluded.

Nothing submitted. No SUBMITTED_* flag touched. No historical artifact rewritten.

