ed a 'nothing fits' answer), the budget->score curve re-priced under M0/M1/M2 through the INSTALLED scorer per-seed matched, and the early-stop lever priced on its BENEFIT side as two trade curves. ANSWER (9h cap, 110 games, margin = 80% of usable): largest MEASURED budget that fits = 2000, and 2000 also survives every cost level; 4000 fits centrally but its cost is EXTRAPOLATED. At the 6h reading it tightens to 1000 central / 400 conservative. Critical N at the 9h cap: 233 games at b400, 141 at b2000 (central). WHAT THE RAISE BUYS: +7 median wins/seed for +0.0541 score points out of 2500 in the OFFLINE unit (3/3 seeds positive, p-floor 0.25 = UNDERPOWERED); in the PAID unit the full-corpus delta (+0.0359) is SMALLER than the attribution estimator's own error (0.0565) so its SIGN IS NOT RESOLVABLE there, and on the 11 (game, seed) cells that carry EXACT attribution at BOTH budgets (5 games, of the 44 exact cells) it is +0.0021 with 8 structural ties. The offline unit also OVERSTATES the raise: M2's optimism grows 2.97% -> 5.54% from b400 to b2000 because the reset charge grows with the budget. THE PRIOR FITTED COST MODEL IS TESTED AND ITS CROSSING POINT VOIDED: its MECHANISM was already falsified by the sibling (cost grows at CONSTANT induction count), and at the LEVEL its projections run 1.68-2.11x above this file's throughput-based cost (227.3 vs 107.8 s/game at b400) because it projects a CONTENDED per-game LATENCY and then multiplies by the game count — double-counting once throughput is measured flat. Its implied crossing point is replaced by the critical-N table. This does NOT impugn either measurement: the K=1 arm reproduces the published UNCONTENDED anchor within its noise floor (ratio median 0.973, range 0.679-1.579 against a published same-config fold of up to 2.468). A validated uniform-rate reset-attribution estimator closes limitation (6) of REQ-ARC-WMTE-5986 at a published accuracy (|rel err| median 1.89%, p90 7.26%, max 13.39% over 44 exact cells). EA